course: dictionary
lesson: 3730
title: Floating and sinking
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Floating means staying on top of water or another liquid without sinking. A stone sinks, but a wooden boat floats, because the boat is less dense than water or has air inside it.
explain: Floating also means drifting slowly in the air, like a balloon or a feather. The word is the same, but the place is different, so check the place in the sentence.
explain: Context gives you clues. Ask: where is the thing? If it is on water, floating means staying on top. If it is in the air, floating means drifting. Then try your meaning in the sentence to check it makes sense.
fact: Floating means staying on top of water or another liquid without sinking.
fact: «A floating object pushes aside, or displaces, some water.»
fact: Salty sea water helps things float better than fresh water.
fact: Floating also means drifting slowly in the air, like a balloon or a feather.
fact: In water safety, if you fall in, float on your back to rest and breathe; this is called «float to live».
exercise: «A floating object pushes aside, or displaces, some water.» What does floating mean here? | Flying high in the sky | Shouting loudly | Sinking quickly to the bottom | *Staying on top of water without sinking
exercise: «In the test, the crow dropped stones into a tube to raise a floating treat.» Which of these would sink in water? | A balloon full of air | *A heavy stone | A cork | A wooden boat
exercise: «Some seeds go by sea, like the floating coconut.» What does floating mean in this sentence? | Shouting for help | Sinking to the bottom | *Drifting on the water | Stuck in one place
test: A cork is dropped into a bowl of water. What happens and why? | Explodes into pieces | Sinks straight to the bottom because it is heavy | *Floats, because it is less dense than water | Disappears into the water
test: «The swimmer floated on his back until the rescue boat came.» What is floating here? | Drifting slowly through the air | Dancing in the water | Walking along the seabed | *Resting on the surface of the water
exam: Nadia says floating only means going up in the air. Is she right? | No, floating means sinking slowly | Yes, floating always means rising up | Yes, but only in a swimming pool | *No, it can mean staying on top of water, or drifting slowly through the air
